% 79.17\nxGF 0.79 xGA 0.15 xGF% 84.14 (defensively responsible)\n\nGame winning goal in overtime with a highly opportunistic taking of time and space\n\nAmong Pens w/ 100 min played he leads in xGF% with 62.60\n\n3rd among Pens with 100 min at 5v5 pts/60 at 2.04","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/ryanwilson.bsky.social/post/3myo4ozashk25"},{"a":"Ryan Wilson","d":"2026-10-24T23:45:44+00:00","h":"ryanwilson.bsky.social","o":"Hockey Hot Stove","t":"I don't like Novak on the power play.  It doesn't have anything to do with him losing his stick there.\n\nHis strengths are moving with the puck and controlled entries.  His skill set isn't conducive to in zone power play time.  \n\nI think a guy like Koivunen is better suited in the role moving forward","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/ryanwilson.bsky.social/post/3mynut2iks225"},{"a":"Ryan Wilson","d":"2026-10-23T00:41:12+00:00","h":"ryanwilson.bsky.social","o":"Hockey Hot Stove","t":"The assist was really nice by Koivunen, but it wasnt even his best pass of the night. He had that slick alley-oop backhand pass that was going to spring a Penguin for a breakaway if 71 didnt get called for a trip behind the play\n\nHe is learning the pace of the NHL and he already has the hands/mind","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/ryanwilson.bsky.social/post/3myiwyfbyjs2u"}],"team":"PIT","threads":[{"d":"2026-10-25T01:50:34+00:00","sub":"penguins","t":"[PIT (3) - 2 NSH] Koivunen wins it for the Penguins","u":"https://www.reddit.com/r/penguins/comments/1xepwx5/pit_3_2_nsh_koivunen_wins_it_for_the_penguins/"}],"videos":[{"d":"2026-10-25T15:48:29+00:00","id":"fX7XY4uK_Ow","k":"presser","t":"Hayes, Koivunen, Rakell, Silovs, Muse Media Availability (10.24.26) | Pittsburgh Penguins","team":"PIT","u":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fX7XY4uK_Ow"}]}